# Copy to .env in this folder (gitignored). `just e2e` loads it for every e2e
# recipe; `ENV=staging just e2e` additionally loads the repo-root .env.staging
# and runs against that deployment's mailbox.

# Wi-Fi networks the e2e fuzz may walk phones and hubs through, as
# ssid:passphrase pairs in the order the moves index them. Leave unset to keep
# every hub and network move out of the runs. Each access point must:
#   - serve DHCP on a subnet of its own (two on the RouterOS default
#     192.168.88.0/24 hand out clashing routes);
#   - use WPA2-PSK, or no security (a bare `ssid` with no passphrase);
#   - need no upstream — a phone on it has no internet, which is the point.
# Neither SSID nor passphrase may contain ':' or ','. The host's Wi-Fi card
# joins these for the length of a networked run, taking every hub with it.
# List test networks only. The network the phones and the host are on
# otherwise — the one with internet — is never named here: every phone spec
# starts by putting the phones back there from wherever an earlier run left
# them. On Linux the harness reads it (name and passphrase) from the host's
# own Wi-Fi connection and joins it by name on Android phones, so they need
# no Wi-Fi saved by hand; see E2E_HOST_WIFI for other hosts.
E2E_WIFI_NETWORKS=dash-test-a:passphraseA,dash-test-b:passphraseB

# The host's own Wi-Fi network, as ssid:passphrase, for a host the harness
# cannot read it from: macOS, or a host on a wire. Without it an Android
# phone falls back to whatever network its user saved, which has to be the
# host's — except a phone whose Wi-Fi only takes suggestions from adb (e.g.
# a Tecno on HiOS 13), which needs it named. Split at the first ':', so the
# passphrase may hold ':' and ','.
# E2E_HOST_WIFI=my-home-wifi:passphrase

# Firebase service-account key for the real-device push spec, relative to the
# repo root. The spec (and the local push server) run whenever the key exists
# and a mobile agent is launched; leave unset to use the in-repo default,
# crates/push-notifications-server/service-account-key.json (gitignored).
# FCM_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_KEY=crates/push-notifications-server/service-account-key.json

# Host IPv4 that phones reach the local mailbox at. Leave unset to let the
# harness pick the LAN interface; set it when it picks the wrong one.
# E2E_HOST_IP=192.168.1.10

# The iroh relay baked into e2e builds of the app and mailbox server. Leave
# unset for the hosted e2e relay; point it at a locally run relay (e.g.
# `iroh-relay --dev`) on machines that cannot reach the hosted one.
# E2E_RELAY_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3340/
